course: dictionary
lesson: 11747
title: Two spellings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can be spelt in two ways and still mean the same thing. «Baguet» and «baguette» are one word with two spellings, and they sound the same when you say them.
explain: The context tells you which meaning is meant. «Mum bought a crunchy baguet from the bakery for our lunch.» Here it is bread. «The ring had a baguet diamond, cut in a long rectangle.» Here it is a gem.
explain: When you meet an unfamiliar spelling, look for a more common spelling in your dictionary. Here, «baguette» is the usual spelling, so look under that word to check the meaning.
fact: «Baguet» is another spelling of «baguette».
fact: A baguette is a long, thin loaf of French bread.
fact: As a gem, a baguette is a small stone cut in a long rectangle shape.
fact: Both spellings sound the same when you read them aloud.
fact: Most of the time you will see «baguette» spelt this way, but «baguet» appears in some menus, old texts and jewellery.
exercise: «Mum bought a crunchy baguet from the bakery.» What is a baguet here? | *A long, thin loaf of French bread | A tall tower of stone | A small, sweet cake | A pair of warm gloves
exercise: «The ring had a baguet diamond, cut in a long rectangle.» What does baguet mean here? | *A gem cut in a long rectangle shape | A soft cushion | A kind of wooden box | A round, bright coin
exercise: Which word is another spelling of baguet? | baggage | bandage | bagel | *baguette
test: «The baguet was still warm when we bought it.» What does baguet mean here? | A ring with a sparkling gem | A kind of hat | A sort of tent | *Long, thin French bread
test: Why do «baguet» and «baguette» mean the same thing? | *They are two spellings of the same word | One is a spelling mistake that nobody uses | One is for food and one is for a boat | They are two different words that sound different
exam: Which statement is true? | «Baguet» is a kind of bird and has nothing to do with bread | *«Baguet» and «baguette» can both mean a long, thin French loaf | Two spellings always mean two different things | «Baguet» means a small round cake and «baguette» means a coin
